{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1678","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1678","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1678\",\"parent_revision\":\"3a8e3ae98c88ea1baebc7945f7838aece25451f7c7fb1fdebd92b5bfd5375805\",\"root_revision\":\"3a8e3ae98c88ea1baebc7945f7838aece25451f7c7fb1fdebd92b5bfd5375805\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nExtend `task_status_hook.py` (the existing `PostToolUse` handler) with a call counter that fires a structured knowledge snapshot every N `PostToolUse` events (default 15). The counter state is maintained in `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/context/tool-call-counter-{session_id}.json` \u2014 the same durable context directory used by the existing active-task file.\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAll conditions resolved:\\n\\n| Condition | Status | Evidence |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `PostToolUse` fires on Write/Edit/Bash | AVAILABLE | Already registered in `hooks.json` for `task_status_hook.py` |\\n| Counter state mechanism | AVAILABLE | Counter file in dh context dir; same pattern as `active-task-{session_id}.json` |\\n| Assistant message content in payload | AVAILABLE (absent) | Not in payload; structural file paths from `tool_input.file_path` do not require JSONL |\\n| N configurable | AVAILABLE | `CLAUDE_SKILLS_SNAPSHOT_INTERVAL` env var; default 15 |\\n| Hook language | AVAILABLE | Python; extends existing `task_status_hook.py` \u2014 no new CJS script needed |\\n| `HookProfile.MINIMAL` skip | AVAILABLE | Line 163 of `task_status_hook.py` already skips PostToolUse; counter logic inherits this |\\n| Session log path | DERIVABLE | Depends on #317 and #775 agreement |\\n</div>\\n\\n## Issue Classification\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Type**: feature \u2014 extends existing `task_status_hook.py` with counter state and conditional snapshot writer  \\n**Design dependency**: session log file path must be agreed with #317 and #775 before writing snapshot output\\n</div>\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Must change:**\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py` \u2014 add counter read/increment/write logic and conditional snapshot writer to existing `PostToolUse` handler; counter file: `tool-call-counter-{session_id}.json` in dh context dir\\n- `tests/test_task_status_hook_profiles.py` \u2014 new tests: counter increment, snapshot trigger, reset\\n\\n**Review (no change expected):**\\n- `plugins/development-harness/hooks/hooks.json` \u2014 no change if counter added to existing `task_status_hook.py`\\n\\n**Reference (read-only during implementation):**\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/hooks-io-api/SKILL.md` \u2014 PostToolUse payload fields\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/hooks-guide/references/claude-session-log-schema-reference.md` \u2014 load before any JSONL reads\\n- `research/context-management/mempalace.md` line 186 \u2014 N=15 default source\\n</div>\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- Session log file path: agree with #317 and #775 before writing snapshot output\\n- Check GitHub for #1376 and verify overlap before implementation\\n- Related: #1677 (PreCompact hook \u2014 complements periodic saves; load together)\\n</div>\\n\\n## Benefits\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- Crash recovery up to N-1 tool calls back without waiting for Stop/SubagentStop\\n- Complements `PreCompact` (#1677): periodic saves fire throughout the session; PreCompact fires only at compression\\n- No latency cost: hook already fires on every Write/Edit/Bash; counter increment adds &lt;10ms\\n- File paths of recently modified files available structurally from `tool_input` \u2014 no JSONL parse required for that data\\n- `HookProfile.MINIMAL` automatically skips via existing PostToolUse skip rule\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Counter maintained in `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/context/tool-call-counter-{session_id}.json`; resets at `SessionStart`\\n- [ ] Snapshot fires when counter reaches N; N defaults to 15, overridable via `CLAUDE_SKILLS_SNAPSHOT_INTERVAL`\\n- [ ] Snapshot appended as JSONL line to session log file (path compatible with #317 and #775)\\n- [ ] Each record contains: ISO timestamp, `session_id`, active task ID (from context file), list of `tool_name` values since last snapshot, `trigger: \\\"periodic\\\"`\\n- [ ] File paths of recently modified files extracted from `tool_input.file_path` in Write/Edit calls (structural extraction, no JSONL parse)\\n- [ ] Counter write uses temp-file-swap pattern (no silent data loss on write failure)\\n- [ ] `HookProfile.MINIMAL` skips counter logic (inherits existing PostToolUse skip at line 163)\\n- [ ] Tests added to `tests/test_task_status_hook_profiles.py`: counter increment, snapshot trigger at N, reset at SessionStart\\n- [ ] Hook exits 0 on success and when counter has not yet reached N; never exits 2\\n- [ ] Load `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/hooks-guide/references/claude-session-log-schema-reference.md` before implementing any `transcript_path` JSONL reads\\n</div>\\n\\n## Effort\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**STANDARD** \u2014 extends `task_status_hook.py` with counter state (same pattern as existing context file), conditional snapshot write, and tests. No new scripts required unless counter logic is separated into its own module.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want **a periodic knowledge snapshot that fires every N tool calls and appends structured state to a session log file** so that **crash recovery does not require waiting for a Stop or SubagentStop event**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research entry: `./research/context-management/mempalace.md` \u2014 pattern: Save Hook (Section 7: Auto-Save Hooks)\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-08\\n- **Groomed**: 2026-04-09\\n</div>\\n\\n## Research Resolution\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**What data does a `PostToolUse` hook receive?**\\nConfirmed in `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/hooks-io-api/SKILL.md` lines 59\u201377. Payload: `session_id`, `transcript_path`, `cwd`, `permission_mode`, `hook_event_name`, `tool_name`, `tool_input`, `tool_response`, `tool_use_id`. **Assistant message content is NOT in the payload.** To extract decisions or reasoning, the hook must read `transcript_path` JSONL. File paths of recently modified files are available structurally from `tool_input.file_path` on Write/Edit calls \u2014 no JSONL parsing required for that subset.\\n\\n**Can a hook maintain state (call counter) across invocations?**\\nNo native counter in the payload. Each invocation is stateless. Counter must be maintained in a file. Pattern: read counter file \u2192 increment \u2192 write \u2192 conditionally fire snapshot. Counter resets at `SessionStart`. `CLAUDE_SKILLS_SNAPSHOT_INTERVAL` env var controls N (default 15, matching the documented MemPalace default from `research/context-management/mempalace.md` line 186).\\n\\n**Relationship to backlog #1376:**\\nIssue #1376 was not found in the local backlog cache. Closest local items: #317 (structured session work logs), #775 (persistent structured session metadata), #113 (multi-session build state lost during compaction). Check GitHub for #1376 and verify overlap before implementation begins.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"7f095b23f019be6ddf443f4cc7f43cce30293facacb3dc2bbc9d9965b20d879b\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABSdriNw\"}"}